# T-001: Initialize Project Knowledge

## Goal

Replace template placeholders with the first concrete project brief, scope,
non-goals, success criteria, and first useful vertical slice.

## Context

The generated project starts with enough definition to work safely. Capture the
problem, target user, desired outcome, critical constraints, and first
hypothesis before or alongside the smallest useful implementation slice.

## Scope

- Update project brief, requirements, roadmap, and generated status dashboards
  with only the knowledge needed for the first slice.
- Identify the smallest useful vertical slice that can test the project
  hypothesis.

## Out of Scope

- Exhaustive roadmap or full requirements definition.
- Production runtime.
- External services or infrastructure.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `project/brief.md` names the problem, target user, desired outcome, critical constraints, and first useful vertical slice.
- [ ] `project/roadmap.md` has only the current near-term direction needed for the first slice.
- [ ] `project/requirements.md` contains concrete and verifiable requirements for the current slice.
- [ ] `make sync-project-docs` and `make validate-project` pass.

## Verification

Run:

```bash
make sync-project-docs
make validate-project
```

## Documentation Impact

Project knowledge documents and generated dashboards will be updated.

## Completion Notes

Pending.

## Notes

Do not wait for exhaustive definition. Build the smallest useful slice once the
critical context and constraints are clear enough to keep the work safe.
